## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: fry, Language: Western Frisian, Number of verses: 121
## References: Hoekstra, Jarich. 2011. Meervoudsvorming in het Westerlauwers Fries en het Nederlands (en patroniemvorming in het Noord-Fries). Taal en tongval. 63. 281-301. 10.5117/TET2011.2.HOEK. ; Immaterieel Erfgoed. n.d. Westfriese taal/dialect. https://www.immaterieelerfgoed.nl/nl/page/2796/westfriese-taal-dialect ; NH Nieuws. 2018. Moet óók West-Fries een officiële taal worden? https://www.nhnieuws.nl/nieuws/232812/moet-west-fries-een-taal-worden ; Sipma, P. 1913. Phonology & grammar of modern West Frisian; with phonetic texts and glossary ; Wichmann, Søren, Eric W. Holman, Cecil H. Brown, Matthew S. Dryer, and Qibin Ran (eds.). 2025. The ASJP Database (version 21).

